React state is a snapshot: calling `setNumber` does not change `number` in the currently running handler. If `number` is `0`, all three calls become `setNumber(1)`. React also batches the updates and processes them after the handler finishes, so the next value is `1`, not `3`.[4][5]

Use updater functions so each update receives the pending result of the previous one:[1][2]

```js
setNumber(n => n + 1);
setNumber(n => n + 1);
setNumber(n => n + 1);
```

React queues these functions and processes them in order during the next render, producing `1`, then `2`, then `3`.[1][2]

